{
  "_doc": [
    "Identity pools for the web hierarchy viewer. Name + avatar are a DISPLAY LABEL",
    "assigned by the viewer - nothing is stored anywhere and no agent knows its own",
    "name. format.mjs assigns names[i] by spawn order within an agentType, recomputed",
    "from the transcripts on every refresh, so the mapping is deterministic and stable",
    "across server restarts. 30 names per role: a session would need 30 concurrent",
    "agents of one role before the pool cycles and a repeat takes a ² suffix.",
    "",
    "This file is a COMMON artifact: invented display names and generic robot art,",
    "no real person's data anywhere. An adopter takes it as-is or replaces it whole;",
    "format.mjs reads it unless config.json's identities.file names another roster.",
    "",
    "avatar    = the role's silhouette, worn by every name without a portrait.",
    "portraits = optional bespoke art for a name. Most names have none, so most",
    "            agents wear the role silhouette - the avatar always identifies",
    "            the ROLE, the name always identifies the AGENT. Art paths resolve",
    "            against this file's directory.",
    "names     = ordered; position i is assigned to the i-th agent of that role.",
    "            Order is load-bearing: never reorder or insert mid-list, or every",
    "            past session's graph silently renames. Append only.",
    "",
    "Types absent from this file render with no name and no avatar from THIS roster",
    "(that includes the synthetic root session, which is the human",
    "operator's, not an agent - the root block is instead labelled with its fleet",
    "member by format.mjs's fleetName(), which reads config.json's fleet.by_config_dir",
    "for the running CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, not this file).",
    "",
    "Art: generic robot illustrations. A role's silhouette is one of the",
    "ephemeral-*.png family (a blank face); a portrait is a bespoke robot. Every",
    "name is unique across ALL roles, so a name alone identifies an agent."
  ],

